 "missing_frames": [],
 "arc": "A weight shift with a twist through the middle. The step is small and the engine is the pelvis turning against the shoulders: weight rolls onto the character-right foot, the hips rotate character-left, and the ribcage stays facing front so the torso wrings. The rise onto the balls of both feet is the anticipation; the twist is the action; the settle back through the heels is the follow-through.\n\nThe character-right arm climbs from waist to above shoulder height across the second half as the twist unwinds, while the character-left arm stays low and still — the asymmetry is the whole look of the move.\n\nLoop seam: frame 15 is on the character-left foot, mirroring frame 0's weight over the character-left side, so the loop reads as the next weight change rather than a reset.",
